 "descriptions": {
  "kiwi_turnip_sysmem": "With a custom Turnip driver (Lemon-Ade), render in sysmem mode instead of GMEM tiles (TU_DEBUG=sysmem). Automatic turns it on for Adreno 8xx, where GMEM hangs the GPU in Halo 4 and Forza 4 and sysmem costs nothing measurable. No effect on the system driver.",
  "kiwi_vulkan_queue_priority": "Global priority asked for the graphics queue. auto requests none (as default). realtime puts the emulator in the GPU's top ring: fewer preemptions on Turnip, but the app's own UI can stall behind it and Android may report the app as not responding. high preempts more than default on the Adreno 830.",
  "occlusion_query": "Occlusion query mode for EVENT_WRITE_ZPD (lens flares, culling, auto exposure). strict waits for the real GPU result (default, most accurate); fast and fast-alt don't wait and use a cached result; fake writes a fixed result without asking the GPU. fast or fake can help games that stall on queries.",
  "depth_transfer_not_equal_test": "Use the not-equal depth test when copying depth between render targets. Off fixes some wrong depth after transfers (GTA V light-cone wedges on Adreno) at a small cost."
 }
